public import WeilConjectures.RingTheory.CohenMacaulay.Basic

/-!
# Miracle flatness

*Miracle flatness* is the local criterion for flatness of a local homomorphism `f : R →+* S` of
Noetherian local rings whose source is regular, whose target is Cohen–Macaulay and whose fibre
ring `S ⧸ m_R S` has dimension exactly `dim S - dim R`: under these hypotheses `f` is flat.

## Main definitions and results

* `RingHom.fiberRing`: the fibre ring `S ⧸ m_R S` of a local homomorphism `f : R →+* S`.
* `RingHom.QuasiFinite.ringKrullDim_fiberRing_eq_zero`: the fibre ring of a quasi-finite local
  homomorphism is zero dimensional. This is the hypothesis on the fibre that a finite, or more
  generally a locally quasi-finite, morphism of schemes supplies.
* `RingHom.Flat.of_ringKrullDim_eq_add_fiberRing`: miracle flatness. **This is stated with a
  deliberate `sorry`**; see the `TODO` below.
* `RingHom.Flat.of_ringKrullDim_eq_add_of_ker_eq`: the same criterion with the fibre ring
  presented as an arbitrary quotient of `S` by `m_R S`, which is the form a geometric consumer
  meets: the local ring of the scheme-theoretic fibre comes with a surjection from `𝒪_{X,x}`
  rather than as a literal quotient type.

## Design

The fibre ring is spelled `S ⧸ (maximalIdeal R).map f` rather than `S ⊗[R] ResidueField R`: both
the criterion and its consumers only ever use the Krull dimension of the fibre, and the quotient
is the presentation for which `ringKrullDim` is directly computable. For a morphism of schemes
`f : X ⟶ Y` and `x : X` with `y = f x`, this quotient of the stalk map is the local ring
`𝒪_{X_y, x}` of the scheme-theoretic fibre, which is how the blueprint states the hypothesis.

The hypotheses of the blueprint statement that `f` be locally of finite type and that the schemes
be locally Noetherian are not needed here: `IsRegularLocalRing` and `IsCohenMacaulayLocalRing`
already carry Noetherianity of the two local rings, which is all the criterion uses.

## TODO

Prove `RingHom.Flat.of_ringKrullDim_eq_add_fiberRing`. The standard route runs by induction on
`dim R`, using that a regular local ring is a domain and that a regular system of parameters of
`R` maps to a sequence in `S` which is regular because `S` is Cohen–Macaulay of the expected
dimension; mathlib `v4.33.1` has neither the Cohen–Macaulay condition (supplied by
`WeilConjectures.RingTheory.CohenMacaulay.Basic`) nor any of the flatness criteria that feed into
it — neither the local criterion of flatness nor the dimension inequality
`dim S ≤ dim R + dim (S ⧸ m_R S)` for a local homomorphism of Noetherian local rings.

## References

* [Matsumura, *Commutative ring theory*, §23][MatsumuraCRT]
* The section *Flatness and dimension* of the chapter *Commutative algebra* of
  [the Stacks project][stacks-project].

## Blueprint

This file states `prop:deg-miracle-flatness` of the curve-estimates blueprint at the level of
rings; `WeilConjectures.AlgebraicGeometry.MiracleFlatness` transfers it to schemes.
-/

@[expose] public section

open IsLocalRing

universe u v

variable {R : Type u} {S : Type v} [CommRing R] [CommRing S]

/-- The *fibre ring* of a local homomorphism `f : R →+* S` of local rings: the quotient of `S` by
the ideal generated by the image of the maximal ideal of `R`.

For `f` the stalk map of a morphism of schemes `f : X ⟶ Y` at a point `x` with image `y = f x`,
this is the local ring `𝒪_{X_y, x}` of the scheme-theoretic fibre `X_y` at `x`. -/
abbrev RingHom.fiberRing [IsLocalRing R] (f : R →+* S) : Type v :=
  S ⧸ (maximalIdeal R).map f

/-- The fibre ring of a **quasi-finite** local homomorphism of local rings is zero dimensional.

The fibre ring is a finite-dimensional algebra over the residue field of the source, hence
Artinian, hence of Krull dimension zero. This is the hypothesis on the fibre that a finite, or
more generally a locally quasi-finite, morphism of schemes supplies for the miracle-flatness
criterion. -/
theorem RingHom.QuasiFinite.ringKrullDim_fiberRing_eq_zero [IsLocalRing R] [IsLocalRing S]
    {f : R →+* S} [IsLocalHom f] (hf : f.QuasiFinite) :
    ringKrullDim f.fiberRing = 0 := by
  let : Algebra R S := f.toAlgebra
  have : Algebra.QuasiFinite R S := hf
  have hmap : (maximalIdeal R).map f ≤ maximalIdeal S :=
    ((local_hom_TFAE f).out 0 2 rfl rfl).mp ‹_›
  have hne : (maximalIdeal R).map f ≠ ⊤ :=
    (hmap.trans_lt (maximalIdeal.isMaximal S).lt_top).ne
  have : Nontrivial f.fiberRing := Ideal.Quotient.nontrivial_iff.mpr hne
  let : Algebra (ResidueField R) f.fiberRing :=
    (Ideal.Quotient.lift (maximalIdeal R)
      ((Ideal.Quotient.mk ((maximalIdeal R).map f)).comp f)
      fun _ ha ↦ Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.mpr (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem f ha)).toAlgebra
  have : IsScalarTower R (ResidueField R) f.fiberRing :=
    IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq fun _ ↦ rfl
  have : Algebra.QuasiFinite (ResidueField R) f.fiberRing :=
    Algebra.QuasiFinite.of_restrictScalars R _ _
  have : Module.Finite (ResidueField R) f.fiberRing :=
    Algebra.QuasiFinite.iff_of_isArtinianRing.mp inferInstance
  have : IsArtinianRing f.fiberRing := .of_finite (ResidueField R) _
  have : Ring.KrullDimLE 0 f.fiberRing :=
    .mk₀ fun I hI ↦ (IsArtinianRing.isPrime_iff_isMaximal I).mp hI
  exact ringKrullDimZero_iff_ringKrullDim_eq_zero.mp inferInstance

/-- **Miracle flatness**: a local homomorphism `f : R →+* S` of Noetherian local rings with `R`
regular, `S` Cohen–Macaulay and `dim S = dim R + dim (S ⧸ m_R S)` is flat.

This is stated with a deliberate `sorry`: it is the only unproved statement of this development,
and everything else in this file and in
`WeilConjectures.AlgebraicGeometry.MiracleFlatness` is deduced from it. See the `TODO` in the
module docstring for the ingredients mathlib is missing, and
[Matsumura, §23][MatsumuraCRT] or the section *Flatness and dimension* of the *Commutative
algebra* chapter of the Stacks project for the proof. -/
theorem RingHom.Flat.of_ringKrullDim_eq_add_fiberRing (f : R →+* S) [IsLocalHom f]
    [IsRegularLocalRing R] [IsCohenMacaulayLocalRing S]
    (h : ringKrullDim S = ringKrullDim R + ringKrullDim f.fiberRing) :
    f.Flat :=
  sorry

/-- **Miracle flatness**, with the fibre ring presented as an arbitrary quotient of `S` by the
ideal generated by the image of the maximal ideal of `R`.

This is the form a geometric consumer meets: the local ring of the scheme-theoretic fibre of a
morphism at a point comes with a surjection from the local ring of the source, not as a literal
quotient type. -/
theorem RingHom.Flat.of_ringKrullDim_eq_add_of_ker_eq {T : Type*} [CommRing T] (f : R →+* S)
    [IsLocalHom f] [IsRegularLocalRing R] [IsCohenMacaulayLocalRing S] (g : S →+* T)
    (hg : Function.Surjective g) (hker : RingHom.ker g = (maximalIdeal R).map f)
    (h : ringKrullDim S = ringKrullDim R + ringKrullDim T) :
    f.Flat := by
  have he : ringKrullDim T = ringKrullDim f.fiberRing :=
    ringKrullDim_eq_of_ringEquiv
      ((RingHom.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective hg).symm.trans (Ideal.quotEquivOfEq hker))
  exact RingHom.Flat.of_ringKrullDim_eq_add_fiberRing f (by rw [h, he])
